    }), "\n", _jsx(_components.p, {
      children: "Tools do not create process; they support it. This distinction matters because teams frequently adopt a tool hoping it will solve a process problem, and are then surprised when the problem persists. Incident.io does not create a postmortem culture - it reduces the friction of running a postmortem for a team that already has the discipline. Backstage does not create service ownership - it makes ownership visible for a team that has already assigned it. Conventional Commits does not improve release communication - it automates the capture of communications a team was already making manually."
    }), "\n", _jsx(_components.p, {
